        "original_id": "d3d8f9db-1ce9-51bd-b511-e5f27b0a29e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pacchimiriam Adiyappa, Ghanam Krishna Iyer, Shahuji II Bhonsle, Serfoji I\n- Places: Thanjavur, Tamil Nadu\n- Organizations: Maratha kingdom of Thanjavur, Bhonsle dynasty\n- Roles: court musician, ruler, composer, student\n- Topics: South Indian religion, art, architecture\n\nFacts:\n- Pacchimiriam Adiyappa was a famous court musician at the Maratha kingdom of Thanjavur in the 18th century.\n- Shahuji II Bhonsle of the Bhonsle dynasty ruled Thanjavur from 1738 to 1739.\n- Shahuji II Bhonsle rose to power based on an unverified claim that he was an illegitimate son of Serfoji I.\n- Thanjavur, formerly called Tanjore, is a city in the south Indian state of Tamil Nadu.\n- Thanjavur is an important center of South Indian religion, art, and architecture.\n- Ghanam Krishna Iyer was a student of the famous composer Pacchimiriam Adiyappa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
